{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975237,"nonce":"QuNxh9I+GHsWiqbrfdikn5RK58k=","title":"no verb can install a MinifiedThing — G5 is ungradeable and quest monuments cannot be started","message":"Nothing in the 144 verbs creates a `Blueprint_Install`, so a minified thing can be bought, hauled and counted but never put down. Found live on openrun-20260909.\n\n## Why this is p1 rather than a convenience\n\n**The run contract grades G5 as `MinifiedThing count == 0`** and standing rule 4 says query it every day (\"Five sculptures sat in a crate for 66 days last run\"). The mod publishes exactly that count — `gauges.stock.uninstalled`, whose own basis line says *\"This is the G5 measure (4c12e5d): the contract grades G5 as count == 0\"*. **The measure ships; the act that would move it does not.** So the moment any minified thing exists, G5 is unreachable by any sequence of verbs.\n\nIt also blocks an accepted quest with a clock running: `The Extensive Edifice` (accepted day 14, 14-day build limit) delivers a `MonumentMarker` as a `MinifiedThing`, and the monument cannot be started without installing it.\n\n## The dead ends, all checked live\n\n    things {def:\"MinifiedThing\", detail:true}\n      -\u003e id 48929, at [108,135], label \"monument marker\", forbidden false\n\n    build {def:\"MonumentMarker\", at:[120,124], dry_run:true}\n      -\u003e bad-args: 'MonumentMarker' is not BuildableByPlayer (designationCategory is null,\n         so no Designator_Build exists for it and it has no blueprintDef)\n\n    carry {pawn:805, thing:48929}\n      -\u003e bad-args: carry accepts 'pawn', 'pawns', 'queue' and 'target'\n\n`build` is the right shape but wrong path: installing is not `Designator_Build`, it is `Designator_Install` over an existing minified thing.\n\n## The gate to reproduce\n\nThe player's route is `RimWorld/Designator_Install`, whose `CanDesignateCell` / `DesignateSingleCell` end in `GenConstruct.PlaceBlueprintForInstall(MinifiedThing, IntVec3, Map, Rot4, Faction)`. Two facts this codebase has already established and should reuse rather than rediscover:\n\n- `Source/AutoRimmer/ConstructionSkill.cs` (~line 43 and ~277): `ThingDefGenerator_Buildings` attaches the skill requirement onto the blueprint only `if (!isInstallBlueprint)`, so **a `Blueprint_Install` has NO construction skill gate**. A colony with Construction 2 can install anything.\n- `Source/AutoRimmer/ConstructionVerbs.cs` (~line 956): `Blueprint_Install.TotalMaterialCost()` is empty — installing costs no materials.\n\nSo the refusals are placement and reachability, not skill or cost.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `install {pawn?, thing, at, rot?}` places an install blueprint for a spawned `MinifiedThing` through `GenConstruct.PlaceBlueprintForInstall`, never by spawning the building directly.\n- It reproduces `Designator_Install`'s own preconditions and cites them: the cell must accept the building (`GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt`), the minified thing must be reachable and not forbidden to the installer, and an existing install blueprint for the same thing must not be double-placed.\n- `dry_run` previews, matching `build`.\n- After a colonist completes it, `gauges.stock.uninstalled.count` drops and `goals.G5.ok` becomes true. **That is the acceptance that matters** — the gauge already exists, so this closes the loop the contract grades on.\n- A minified thing installed onto an illegal cell is refused with the game's own reason, not silently relocated.\n- Installing a `MonumentMarker` from a quest lets the monument's own build sequence begin.","files":null}]}